OpenGL Assignment 1

Student IT-2506: Abdrakhmanov ILnur
Assignment: 1

Description:

This assignment contains four OpenGL programs.

1. red_triangle.cpp
   Displays a single red triangle.

2. blue_square.cpp
   Displays a single blue square.

3. polygons.cpp
   Displays a 2D scene containing:
   - a circle generated using the parametric circle equation;
   - an ellipse;
   - a color-interpolated triangle;
   - a square with multiple color bands.

4. creative.cpp
   Displays a creative 2D OpenGL scene containing:
   - a red horizontal ellipse;
   - a color-interpolated triangle;
   - a shaded dark-red circle;
   - concentric black and white squares.

OpenGL

The programs use modern OpenGL 3.3 Core Profile.

Deprecated OpenGL functions such as glBegin(), glEnd(),
glVertex*(), glColor*(), and fixed-function matrix operations
are not used.

The vertex and color information is passed to the shaders using vertex attributes.

Libraries:
The programs use:
- GLFW
- GLAD
- OpenGL 3.3 Core Profile

Window size: The programs use a 500 x 500 pixel window.

Testing:
Windows 11
Visual Studio
OpenGL 3.3 Core Profile
